 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "PStack() creates the structure holding only version 0, the empty stack. Versions are immutable stacks named by integers. push(version, val) creates a new version equal to that version with val on top and returns its number; the k-th push call returns k. pop(version) returns the number of the version that the given version was pushed onto, that is, the stack without its top. peek(version) returns the top value of that version. size(version) returns its number of elements. Every version passed exists; pop and peek are only called on non-empty versions. Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; each call runs in O(1).",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
